From: OntoDB Team <dev@ontodb.ai>
Subject: [PATCH] Fix NULL deref when CCtx workspace reservation fails

ZSTD_resetCCtx_internal() and ZSTD_reset_matchState() call
ZSTD_cwksp_reserve_*() and store the results without checking
ZSTD_cwksp_reserve_failed() before using the pointers. When a workspace
reservation fails (e.g. under memory pressure while the CCtx workspace is
rebuilt), those pointers stay NULL but the function still returns 0 and
sets initialized = 1.

The next compression writes through the NULL pointers — most visibly in
ZSTD_seqToCodes() via seqStore.llCode/mlCode/ofCode — and crashes.

Several reservation sites are immediately followed by ZSTD_memset() on the
reserved pointer (ldm hashTable, ldm bucketOffsets, CDict tagTable), so
they crash inside the reset functions before any later check could run.

Note: ZSTD_cwksp_reserve_internal() returns NULL for a zero-byte reserve
without setting allocFailed. Checks therefore use the sticky
ZSTD_cwksp_reserve_failed() flag rather than a bare `ptr == NULL` test,
which would mis-classify legitimate zero-size reserves (e.g. hashTable3
when hashLog3 == 0) as failures.

Related: https://github.com/facebook/zstd/issues/3950 (same crash site;
that report covers uninitialized workspace contents. This patch covers
unchecked reservation failure.)

---
 lib/compress/zstd_compress.c | 39 +++++++++++++++++++---
 tests/wksp_alloc_fail_test.c | 403 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 438 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
diff --git a/lib/compress/zstd_compress.c b/lib/compress/zstd_compress.c
index 8245154..1320fb5 100644
--- a/lib/compress/zstd_compress.c
+++ b/lib/compress/zstd_compress.c
@@ -141,8 +141,11 @@ ZSTD_CCtx* ZSTD_initStaticCCtx(void* workspace, size_t workspaceSize)
